// Title: Remote Code Execute via Winrm.vbs
// Sigma ID: 9df0dd3a-1a5c-47e3-a2bc-30ed177646a0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Julia Fomina, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-07 | Modified: 2023-03-03
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects an attempt to execute code or create service on remote host via winrm.vbs.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/bohops/status/994405551751815170
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/lateral-movement-winrm-wmi/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Scripts/Winrm/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_winrm_execution_via_scripting_api_winrm_vbs.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "cscript.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "winrm" and ProcessCommandLine contains "invoke Create wmicimv2/Win32_" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-r:http")
